qa:ATM-QA-AG19-001
    a qa:Finding ;
    qa:findingId "ATM-QA-AG19-001" ;
    qa:phase "phase-AG" ;
    qa:title "execute_remote_ack_reply_plan deleted by name only, logic inlined" ;
    qa:severity "blocking" ;
    qa:pattern "rename-not-remove" ;
    qa:repeatable true ;
    qa:sourceReviewers "req-qa (ARCH-AG19-001)", "arch-qa (ARCH-AG19-001)", "ruthless-boundary-qa (RBQA-F001)" ;
    qa:description """execute_ack_reply_plan (crates/atm-core/src/ack/mod.rs) still contains a dedicated remote-ack execution branch: `if let SendRequestRoute::Remote(remote_host) = route_send_request(&reply.reply_request) { ... deliver_remote_send_request(...) ... }`. Only the standalone function name execute_remote_ack_reply_plan was deleted in AG.19; its logic was inlined verbatim under the new call site rather than being routed through the canonical outbound send executor (execute_delivery_plan / send_mail_with_runtime_and_post_send_emitter) that ordinary sends use. Sprint AG19's own required validation command -- `rg -n \"execute_remote_ack_reply_plan|commit_source_ack_state|route_send_request\\\\(&reply.reply_request\\\\)|AckReplyStateMachine|build_reply_delivery_plan|reply_post_send_messages\" crates/atm-core/src/ack/mod.rs` (docs/plans/phase-AG/sprint-AG19.md:242) -- run verbatim, still matches `route_send_request(&reply.reply_request)` in this file, proving the sprint's own closure gate was never satisfied. Fix: delete the dedicated remote-ack branch entirely; route the ack reply's SendRequest through the same canonical outbound send executor ordinary send uses.""" ;
    qa:sweepScope "repeatable sweep across AG.19-AG.21 for any remaining dedicated remote-ack branching outside the canonical send path" ;
    qa:entangledWith "AG18-QA-002", "AG18-QA-003 (SendResponseEnvelope / dispatch-fork defect family)" .

