# --- Promotion determination ---

qa:ATM-QA-AG19-001-promotion
    a qa:PromotionDecision ;
    qa:finding qa:ATM-QA-AG19-001 ;
    qa:highestOpenBranch "feature/pAG-s21-collapse-dispatch-routing" ;
    qa:promoteToBranch "feature/pAG-s21-collapse-dispatch-routing" ;
    qa:rationale """The defect originates at AG.19 and is carried forward unchanged through AG.20 and AG.21 (all three at identical ack/mod.rs:669-695 line range). AG.18 predates the defect entirely (still has the named function) and is separately FAIL/entangled on AG18-QA-002/QA-003 (SendResponseEnvelope split). Per repeatable-pattern policy and strict earliest-to-latest branch order, the fix is dispatched once to the highest (latest) branch carrying the defect with real commits -- feature/pAG-s21-collapse-dispatch-routing -- and closed on AG.19/AG.20 via merge-forward, not via separate per-branch fix dispatch. AG.21 is dev-in-progress and its own stated scope (collapsing dispatch routing) directly overlaps this fix surface, reinforcing dispatch to that branch rather than an earlier one. This finding is entangled with AG18-QA-002/QA-003's SendResponseEnvelope/dispatch-fork defect family per the same routing-collapse work in AG.21; per project policy (batched QA, no per-sprint fix dispatch until the full sprint batch is triaged), do not dispatch in isolation -- aggregate with the AG18 findings before assigning to arch-ctm. AG.22-AG.25 are not yet started and are excluded from this sweep; re-sweep required once they carry real commits.""" .
